# Exam track — Theme: Family & Myself — Sub-lesson 2: Key Phrases
# Plain sentences (no @question): presented in either direction.
# Mixed with the vocabulary these phrases lean on, so sessions alternate
# word-match and sentence-builder slots.

@lesson F1.02 "Family Phrases"

@word d'Haus = house
@word d'Wunneng = apartment
@word d'Spidol = hospital
@word d'Schoul = school
@word d'Büro = office
@word d'Duerf = village
@word de Weekend = weekend
@word all Dag = every day
@word zesummen = together
@word bei = at (someone's)
@word méi jonk = younger
@word méi al = older

@sentence
@lu Ech hunn zwee Bridder an eng Schwëster.
@en I have two brothers and one sister.
@distractor-lu keng
@distractor-lu véier
@distractor-en four
@distractor-en uncles

@sentence
@lu Meng Schwëster ass méi jonk wéi ech.
@en My sister is younger than me.
@distractor-lu al
@distractor-lu Brudder
@distractor-en older
@distractor-en brother

@sentence
@lu Mäi Brudder wunnt zu Esch.
@en My brother lives in Esch.
@distractor-lu schafft
@distractor-lu meng
@distractor-en works
@distractor-en sister

@sentence
@lu Meng Grousseltere wunnen um Land.
@en My grandparents live in the countryside.
@distractor-lu Stad
@distractor-lu mäin
@distractor-en city
@distractor-en parents

@sentence
@lu Mir iessen all Sonndeg bei menger Groussmamm.
@en We eat at my grandmother's every Sunday.
@distractor-lu Samschdeg
@distractor-lu kachen
@distractor-en Saturday
@distractor-en cook

@sentence
@lu Meng Mamm schafft an engem Spidol.
@en My mother works in a hospital.
@distractor-lu wunnt
@distractor-lu Schoul
@distractor-en lives
@distractor-en school

@sentence
@lu Ech si bestuet an hunn zwee Kanner.
@en I am married and have two children.
@distractor-lu eleng
@distractor-lu dräi
@distractor-en single
@distractor-en three

@sentence
@lu Meng Duechter geet an d'Schoul.
@en My daughter goes to school.
@distractor-lu mäin
@distractor-lu Aarbecht
@distractor-en son
@distractor-en work

@sentence
@lu Mir wunnen zesummen an enger Wunneng.
@en We live together in an apartment.
@distractor-lu Haus
@distractor-lu eleng
@distractor-en house
@distractor-en alone

@sentence
@lu Mäi Cousin wunnt an engem klengen Duerf.
@en My cousin lives in a small village.
@distractor-lu Stad
@distractor-lu grousse
@distractor-en city
@distractor-en big

@sentence
@lu De Weekend gi mir bei meng Elteren.
@en At the weekend we go to my parents'.
@distractor-lu Méindeg
@distractor-lu Kanner
@distractor-en Monday
